    "_profile_metadata": {
        "name": "Cerebellar Cortex - Simplified",
        "description": "Neuron model: HODGKIN_HUXLEY (dt=0.05ms, HH_CEREBELLAR_PURKINJE preset). Simplified cerebellar cortex: 75% granule-like excitatory cells, 25% Purkinje/interneuron inhibition. Purkinje HH preset features high g_Na (75 mS/cm²), prominent CaT current (1.8 mS/cm²) for complex spike-like Ca²⁺ events, and M-current for spike frequency adaptation. Very fast AMPA decay (2ms) reflecting parallel fiber synapses. Strongly facilitating STP (U=0.1, tau_f=300ms) characteristic of parallel fiber→Purkinje cell synapses (Atluri & Regehr 1996). NMDA DISABLED — parallel fiber synapses are primarily AMPA-mediated. Strong LTD-biased STDP (A-/A+=3:1) reflecting cerebellar LTD as the dominant learning rule (Ito 2001). Low connectivity_k=6 reflecting sparse parallel fiber activation.",
        "literature": [
            "Atluri & Regehr 1996 — Parallel fiber facilitation (U≈0.1, tau_f~300ms)",
            "Ito 2001 — Cerebellar LTD as error-driven motor learning",
            "Billings et al. 2014 — Cerebellar STDP: anti-Hebbian LTD dominance",
            "Eccles et al. 1967 — Cerebellar circuit: granule→Purkinje parallel fibers",
            "D'Angelo & De Zeeuw 2009 — Cerebellar timing and synaptic parameters"
        ],
